" data-to=\"hormones-101\">Start charting with Hormones 101 &nbsp;\u2192</a></p></div>`;\n    }\n    if (t.has('dk')) {\n      h += `<div class=\"block\"><p class=\"soft\" style=\"margin:0\">Not sure how long your cycle is? That's really common. Tracking it for a few months is the easiest first step, and it makes any conversation with your doctor much easier. <a href=\"${HUB}access-hormones-101\" data-to=\"hormones-101\">Hormones 101 &amp; Cycle Charts &nbsp;\u2192</a></p></div>`;\n    }\n    h += `<div class=\"block dark\"><p class=\"label\">Your first steps</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 14px\">Next, look at the common disruptors. The groups that match your answers are marked.</p><div class=\"btns\"><a class=\"pill-btn dark\" href=\"#hp-first\">See where to start &nbsp;\u2193</a><a class=\"pill-btn\" href=\"${HUB}coaching\" data-coaching>Work with me &nbsp;\u2192</a></div></div>`;\n    h += '</div>';\n    $('#hp-res').innerHTML = h;\n\n    // mark the disruptor groups that match the answers\n    const yours = {sleep: L.has('stress') || L.has('rhythm'), food: L.has('eating') || L.has('sugar'), body: L.has('training')};\n    $$('.dgroup').forEach(g => g.classList.toggle('yours', !!yours[g.dataset.group]));\n\n    quiz.classList.add('finished');\n    quiz.innerHTML = `<p class=\"label\">Done</p><p class=\"qtext\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">Thank you. Your result is ready below.</p>\n      <div class=\"btns\" style=\"margin-top:14px\"><a class=\"pill-btn dark\" href=\"#hp-result\">See my result &nbsp;\u2193</a><button class=\"pill-btn\" data-go=\"restart\">Start again</button></div>\n      <p class=\"privacy\">${shield}Nothing was saved or sent. If you leave this page, your answers are gone.</p>`;\n    T('result-shown');\n    done.add('hp-check'); done.add('hp-result'); paintSteps();\n    $('#hp-result').scrollIntoView({behavior: 'smooth'});\n  }\n  function clearResult() {\n    quiz.classList.remove('finished');\n    $('#hp-res').innerHTML = '<div class=\"res-empty\">Your result appears here once you\\'ve finished the check.</div>';\n    $$('.dgroup').forEach(g => g.classList.remove('yours'));\n    $('#hp-flags').innerHTML = '';\n  }\n  render();\n\n  /* ---------- disruptor checklist (counts on screen only) ---------- */\n  const boxes = $$('.ticks input');\n  boxes.forEach(b => b.addEventListener('change', () => {\n    const n = boxes.filter(x => x.checked).length, c = $('#hp-dcount');\n    c.hidden = !n;\n    c.textContent = `You checked ${n} of ${boxes.length}`;\n    if (n) { done.add('hp-first'); paintSteps(); }\n  }));\n\n  /* ---------- progress through the seven steps ---------- */\n  const done = new Set(), seen = new Set();\n  const links = $$('.steps a');\n  let now = 'hp-recognize';\n  function paintSteps() {\n    links.forEach(a => { a.classList.toggle('now', a.dataset.step === now); a.classList.toggle('done', done.has(a.dataset.step)); });\n  }\n  const order = links.map(a => a.dataset.step);\n  const io = new IntersectionObserver(es => es.forEach(e => {\n    if (!e.isIntersecting) return;\n    const id = e.target.id;\n    now = id;\n    // reading steps count as done once you've reached them; the check and result once finished\n    order.slice(0, order.indexOf(id) + 1).forEach(x => { if (x !== 'hp-check' && x !== 'hp-result' && x !== 'hp-first') done.add(x); });\n    if (!seen.has(id)) { seen.add(id); T('reached', {at: id.replace('hp-', '')}); }\n    paintSteps();\n  }), {rootMargin: '-40% 0px -55% 0px'});\n  order.forEach(id => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) io.observe(el); });\n  paintSteps();\n\n  /* ---------- clicks ---------- */\n  document.getElementById('hp-recognize').closest('.wrap').addEventListener('click', e => {\n    const a = e.target.closest('a'); if (!a) return;\n    if (a.hasAttribute('data-coaching')) T('coaching-click');\n    else if (a.dataset.to) T('link-click', {to: a.dataset.to});\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</div>\n";
